.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Reconstructs the quantum density of states g(E)=\sum_n\delta(E-E_n) of a unit-mass, unit-frequency harmonic oscillator, V(x)=\tfrac12m\omega^2x^2 with m=\omega=\hbar=1, purely from its classical period T(E) and action S(E), with no reference to the quantum eigenstates themselves (~physicskit.semiclassical.core.gutzwiller.classical_period, gutzwiller_density_of_states). A bound 1D system has exactly one periodic orbit per energy, so Poisson-summing the discrete Bohr-Sommerfeld spectrum over its repetitions r gives an identity that is exact here -- not merely leading order in \hbar:">

